+For a transparent-payload LEO at 600 km altitude serving a UE at 30° elevation (Earth radius 6371 km, f = 20 GHz downlink):
+a) Compute the slant range and one-way UE-satellite propagation delay.
+b) Estimate the worst-case Doppler shift on the service link at this elevation (orbital speed from first principles or state ~7.56 km/s), and the resulting UE requirement.
+c) Explain how NR NTN closes the uplink timing problem: the three timing-advance components and who computes what.
+d) Why does the transparent architecture double-count delay for scheduling, and what parameter absorbs it?
