+a) Slant range d = sqrt((Re sin e)^2 + 2Re*h + h^2) - Re sin e = sqrt(3185.5^2 + 7,645,200 + 360,000) - 3185.5 = sqrt(18,152,610) - 3185.5 ≈ 4260.6 - 3185.5 ≈ **1075 km**; one-way delay = 1075/299792 ≈ **3.6 ms** (service link; the feeder link adds a comparable leg, so UE-gateway one-way ≈ 7-9 ms, RTT ≈ 15-20 ms).
+b) v = sqrt(mu/(Re+h)) = sqrt(398600/6971) ≈ **7.56 km/s**; worst-case fractional Doppler v/c ≈ 25.2 ppm -> at 20 GHz an upper bound ≈ **504 kHz**; at 30° elevation the radial component scales by ~Re cos(e)/(Re+h) ≈ 0.79 -> ≈ **400 kHz**, with high Doppler *rate* during passes. The UE must therefore perform **ephemeris-based pre-compensation** (satellite ephemeris broadcast in SIB; UE with GNSS position computes and pre-corrects frequency/timing).
+c) Uplink timing: **common TA** broadcast per beam/cell (covers the reference-point-to-satellite path), **UE-specific TA** self-computed from GNSS position + ephemeris (UE-satellite geometry), and the **closed-loop TA** fine correction from the network — UE combines all three so PRACH/PUSCH arrive aligned despite hundreds of km of range spread within one beam.
+d) Transparent payload: gNB is on the ground, so scheduling grants and HARQ/RTT timers span **feeder + service** links both ways; **K_offset** (cell-specific, optionally UE-specific update) shifts the UL scheduling timeline to absorb the extra RTT, and HARQ operates with extended/disabled feedback options to survive the delay.
+
+**Grading notes:** Must have: correct slant-range formula and ~1075 km / ~3.6 ms, Doppler upper bound ~500 kHz at 20 GHz with elevation scaling and ephemeris+GNSS pre-compensation, the common/UE-specific/closed-loop TA split, and K_offset's role for the transparent architecture. Accept +-5% arithmetic tolerance and simplified Doppler geometry if stated; accept equivalent terminology for the TA components (UE autonomous/self-estimated TA, network closed-loop correction) — grade concepts over naming. Penalize: using vertical height instead of slant range, GEO-style delay numbers, or omitting UE GNSS dependence.
