+**Cross-link interference and remote interference in TDD**
+
+A nationwide 3.5 GHz TDD network sees sporadic morning uplink desensitization on coastal cells hundreds of km apart. (a) Explain the atmospheric mechanism and why TDD makes it possible for a distant gNB's downlink to hit a victim's uplink despite synchronized frame timing. (b) Describe the 3GPP remote-interference-management concept: what the RIM reference signals establish and the automated workflow between victim and aggressor sets. (c) Separately, define cross-link interference in dynamic/flexible TDD between neighbors, its two component types, and one mitigation for each.
